course: dictionary
lesson: 13228
title: Solid, liquid or gaseous
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Everything around you is made of matter, and matter can be in three main states: solid, liquid or gaseous. A solid holds its shape, a liquid flows and fills the bottom of a container, and a gas spreads out to fill whatever space it is in.
explain: Gaseous is the word for the gas state. Look at the context clues: «Water can be solid, liquid or gaseous.» Solid and liquid are two states, so gaseous must be the third one. Now try the test: swap in "in the form of a gas" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: The word also has a second meaning, like a gas or full of gas. «The fizzy drink was very gaseous» means it was full of bubbles of gas. The clue is the word fizzy, which tells you the drink has gas in it.
fact: Gaseous means in the form of a gas, not a solid or liquid.
fact: Matter has three common states: solid, liquid and gaseous.
fact: «Gaseous oxygen» means oxygen in the form of a gas, like the oxygen you breathe.
fact: Water can be ice (solid), water (liquid) or steam (gaseous).
fact: Gas giants such as Jupiter are called gaseous planets, because they are made mostly of gas.
exercise: «Water can be solid ice, liquid water or gaseous steam.» What does gaseous mean here? | *In the form of a gas | Hard and cold, like ice | Wet and runny, like a puddle | Heavy and dark
exercise: Which of these is a gaseous planet? | Earth's Moon | *Jupiter, a huge planet made mostly of gas | Mars, a small rocky planet | The Sun, which is a star
exercise: Which word means like a gas or full of gas? | frozen | *gaseous | liquid | solid
test: «Ice is solid, but when it melts it becomes liquid, and when it boils it becomes gaseous.» Which state is steam? | Liquid | Frozen | *Gaseous | Solid
test: What does a gaseous state of matter mean? | Matter that is wet and flows | Matter that you can see through only | Matter that is hard and holds its shape | *Matter in the form of a gas
exam: Which is a gaseous substance? | Wooden table | Ice cube | *Oxygen in the air we breathe | Gold ring
